text:
- `diagnostics/`: home-level per-role process logs, codes only: `run-<name>.ndjson`, `hook-<name>.ndjson`, `mcp.ndjson` and `cli-<name>.ndjson`.
 `run` (and `viola revive`'s start arm, which logs as process `run` into `run-<name>.ndjson` with `run`'s detail sink once its strict-modes check has passed; a refused check, on either arm, opens no process log and writes no line), `hook` and the `cli` verbs `verify`, `send`, `wait`, `last`, `list`, `answer`, `pause`, `release`, `revive --list` and `plugin install` have producers today (`cli-<name>.ndjson`: `send` / `wait` / `last` / `answer` / `pause` / `release` — `<name>` the target instance — write `process-start`, the client `channel-request` / `channel-response` lines (`wait`'s carry `after` / `timeout_ms` / `outcome`) and `process-exit{subject:"self"}`, exit 21 with `detail:"instance-dead"` + `during` at WARN, exit 20 with `detail:"wrapper-fault"`; `list`, only under a parsed `VIOLA_NAME` once its scan passed, one `agents-probe` `process-start` / `process-exit` pair per `claude agents --json` read and one `parse-rejected{parser:"claude-agents-json"}` on an oversize or malformed answer (no row text, id, `cwd` or path; chunk 2026-10-16-unwrapped-sessions-on-the-board), and `viola revive`'s start arm writes its `session-live` reading's `agents-probe` pair into `run-<name>.ndjson` and, on a `session-live` refusal, one `process-exit{subject:"self", exit_code:1, detail:"session-live"}`; `viola revive <name> --list`, only under a parsed `VIOLA_NAME` and only after its strict-modes check passed, writes `process-start` and `process-exit{subject:"self"}` (`exit_code` 0 with no detail, or `exit_code` 1 `detail:"no-session"` on an empty chain) into the CALLER's `cli-<VIOLA_NAME>.ndjson`, and with no name opens none (chunk 2026-10-17-cli-machine-contract);
 `viola plugin install`, only under a parsed `VIOLA_NAME` and only after its strict-modes check passed, writes `process-start` and `process-exit{subject:"self"}` into the caller's `cli-<VIOLA_NAME>.ndjson`, and with no name opens none; `verify`'s `process-start`/`process-exit{subject:"self"}` pair, with eight spawn pairs between them — `version-probe` around the `--version` read, `verify-probe` around the print-mode probe and one `verify-pty-probe` pair around each interactive run (Run A, Run B, Run C, Run D, then Run E) and one `agents-probe` pair around Run B's `claude agents --json` read (no row text, prompt, id or path in any line), each `process-start{subject}` then `process-exit{subject, child_exit_status, duration_ms}` from verify's own call-site wrapper (a child of an interactive PTY run killed at a Ctrl-C or TERM stop closes its pair with `duration_ms` and a `child_exit_status`, the PTY pump's exit code, since portable-pty reports a code for a signalled child, as measured at chunk 2026-10-14-resume-and-compact-ledger-rows by its resume-run stop case; a print-mode or `--version` probe child killed at the stop is not measured; a stopped run writes only the pairs it started, and its self exit reads `exit_code:1, detail:"interrupted"`) (`run_bounded` itself stays unlogged, so `run`'s gate keeps its one `version-probe` pair) — all written only when `VIOLA_NAME` holds a valid name; `list`'s (chunk 2026-10-11-the-board-viola-list), also only when `VIOLA_NAME` holds a valid name and only after its strict-modes scan passed: `process-start`, one `parse-rejected{parser:"state-entry", detail:"symlink-ignored"|"malformed", count}` per nonzero scan count (naming no entry), one `state-recovered` per replayed snapshot, one `parse-rejected{parser:"config-json"}` per bad threshold key, and `process-exit{subject:"self"}`;
 with no name, or on a refused scan, `list` opens no `cli-*.ndjson`; `mcp.ndjson` (chunk 2026-10-17-mcp-server-for-drivers), written by `viola mcp` once its home and `diagnostics/` passed `check_path` (a refusal opens no role file and writes no line): `process-start{subject:"self"}`, the Tokio client's `channel-request` / `channel-response` lines, one client-side `send-refused` per refused `send` text, the `list` tool's `agents-probe` pair and the board's `state-recovered` / `parse-rejected` lines (the `config-json` rejections included), and `process-exit` on stdin EOF — none when Claude Code ends it by a signal, as measured live on claude 2.1.287 at that chunk; `hook-<name>.ndjson`: `hook-invoked`, `hook-decision`, `parse-rejected`; `hook`'s drift reports go only to the instance's `diagnostics/detail-hook.ndjson`). One line per `write`; dir 0700, files 0600 on Unix; line format owned by obs and fixed by `schemas/diag-line.v1.json`. Content-bearing detail stays in `instances/<ViolaName>/diagnostics/`.
